      "name": "Our Story Trust Hub",
      "settings": {
        "bg_color": "#ffffff",
        "title": "Our Story in Brief",
        "description": "<p>Fitness Superstore was founded in 2010 to help customers access quality fitness equipment with better value and real support. In 2019, French Fitness launched as our new-equipment brand, giving customers another strong path for building home gyms, studios, schools, hospitality spaces, apartment fitness centers, and commercial facilities. Today, Fitness Superstore helps customers choose between new equipment, including French Fitness, and remanufactured commercial equipment from leading brands.</p>",
        "padding_top": 60,
        "padding_bottom": 60,
        "padding_top_mobile": 32,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 32
      }
    },
    "faq_trusthub_DMdQFp": {
      "type": "faq-trusthub",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_xQcYCJ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "Do you sell both new and remanufactured fitness equipment?",
            "copy": "<p>Yes. Fitness Superstore sells new equipment, including French Fitness and selected new brands, plus remanufactured commercial equipment from leading brands. Many customers combine both paths to get the right balance of appearance, performance, budget, and availability.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_aEHNaC": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "What does remanufactured mean at Fitness Superstore?",
            "copy": "<p>Remanufactured means a commercial-grade machine has gone through a complete rebuild process to restore its performance and appearance to a like-new standard. This includes inspection, replacement of worn components, repainting or refinishing, and quality testing before it ships. You get a proven commercial machine at a fraction of the original price, backed by a warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_V4Yai3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "Is French Fitness sold new only?",
            "copy": "<p>Yes. French Fitness equipment is always sold new. It is Fitness Superstore's proprietary brand and is never sold remanufactured.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_RXzWjn": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "Can I visit the showroom before I buy?",
            "copy": "<p>Yes. Our public showroom is located at 457 Industrial Way in Benicia, California. You can view and compare select equipment in person, test machines when available, and speak with available team members. For the best experience, we recommend calling ahead or requesting a walkthrough so our team can help coordinate support. If you are not local, you can request a video walkthrough.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_JUiN7g": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "What delivery options do you offer?",
            "copy": "<p>We offer curbside delivery, garage delivery, room-of-choice delivery, and delivery with assembly. If you're in Northern California, direct delivery from our Benicia warehouse may also be available depending on your location.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_L8Uxad": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "What warranty comes with remanufactured equipment?",
            "copy": "<p>Remanufactured machines include 1-year parts and labor coverage, with extended warranty options available up to 5 years.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_VYUzaD": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "What warranty comes with French Fitness?",
            "copy": "<p>French Fitness equipment in core covered categories ships with lifetime frame coverage, 10-year parts, and 1-year labor in the USA and Canada.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4HWHGj": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "general",
            "tab_title": "General Questions",
            "title": "How do I contact Fitness Superstore?",
            "copy": "<p>You can reach our team by phone at +1-925-215-2927 or by email at <a href=\"mailto:sales@fitnesssuperstore.com\" target=\"_blank\">sales@fitnesssuperstore.com</a>. You can also visit us in person at 457 Industrial Way, Benicia, California.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_mxC468": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "company",
            "tab_title": "Company & Brand Questions",
            "title": "Who founded Fitness Superstore?",
            "copy": "<p>Fitness Superstore was founded by Tim French in 2010.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_TDNGkb": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "company",
            "tab_title": "Company & Brand Questions",
            "title": "When was Fitness Superstore founded?",
            "copy": "<p>Fitness Superstore was founded in 2010, with French Fitness launching as its in-house new equipment brand in 2019.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_tMRiBM": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "company",
            "tab_title": "Company & Brand Questions",
            "title": "What is the relationship between Fitness Superstore and French Fitness?",
            "copy": "<p>French Fitness is the proprietary new equipment brand created by Fitness Superstore in 2019. Fitness Superstore is the retailer. French Fitness is the house brand, covering strength and cardio categories with lifetime frame, 10-year parts, and 1-year labor coverage. When you buy French Fitness, you are buying directly from the brand that makes it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4pDxUL": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "tab_handle": "company",
            "tab_title": "Company & Brand Questions",
            "title": "Where is Fitness Superstore based?",
            "copy": "<p>Fitness Superstore is based in Benicia, California. The public showroom is at 457 Industrial Way. Remanufacturing and outbound shipping run through 537 Stone Rd Suite F. Both facilities total 63,500 sq ft.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
